# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Oasis Call Center — frontend environment
#
# Copy to frontend/.env and adjust:
#   cp frontend/.env.example frontend/.env
#
# THREE THINGS TO KNOW ABOUT VITE ENV VARS
#
#   1. BUILD TIME, NOT RUNTIME. Vite inlines these into the JS bundle when
#      `npm run build` runs. Setting them on a running container or in
#      docker-compose `environment:` has NO EFFECT — the value is already
#      baked into the shipped assets. To change one, rebuild the image.
#
#   2. ONLY `VITE_`-PREFIXED VARS ARE EXPOSED. Anything without the prefix is
#      invisible to client code.
#
#   3. EVERYTHING HERE IS PUBLIC. It ships inside the JS bundle any visitor
#      can read. Never put an API key, secret, or credential in this file.
#      All secrets belong in backend/.env.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── API base URL ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Base URL the frontend prefixes onto every /api/... request.
# Read in src/hooks/useCalls.js and src/contexts/AuthContext.jsx as:
#     import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL ?? ''
#
# LEAVE IT EMPTY FOR DOCKER / PRODUCTION.
# An empty value means same-origin relative paths (`/api/calls`), and the
# bundled Nginx proxies /api, /webhook, and /health through to the backend
# container — see frontend/nginx.conf. This is why frontend/Dockerfile builds
# without passing the variable at all.
#
# SET IT FOR LOCAL DEV ONLY.
# `npm run dev` serves on :5173 and there is no proxy in vite.config.js, so the
# frontend must be pointed at the backend explicitly:
#     VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3001
#
# Whichever origin the frontend runs on must also appear in the backend's
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS, or every request is blocked by CORS. The backend already
# defaults to http://localhost:5173, so the pairing above works out of the box.
#
# No trailing slash — it is concatenated directly with paths that begin "/api".
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3001